{
  "id": "beijing-master-tournament",
  "name": "Beijing Master Tournament",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The 2025 Beijing Master Tournament was held at the China International Exhibition Center (Shunyi) in Beijing on 20 and 21 September 2025. It was one of that year's four Master Tournaments (大师赛) in China, in Guangzhou, Hangzhou, Beijing and Shenzhen, whose prizes were Simplified Chinese holo Rare Candy cards stamped with the event and the player's result: a plain copy for a good record (the top 3,000 of the open division's preliminaries, seniors with four wins in their preliminaries and juniors with three wins in their breakthrough round), and Top 64, Top 8, 3rd Place, 2nd Place and Champion copies by final standing. The top finishers also got a Victory Symbol, the Simplified Chinese print of the trophy card of Japan's Champions League, stamped 3rd Place for those who finished third and fourth, 2nd Place or Champion.\n\nBuying designated card products at the tournament's shop came with a Charizard ex with its logo. Eight basic Energy cards with the tournament's logo are listed here too. At Guangzhou and Shenzhen such Energy cards came one to an event pack given to entrants, and these are thought to have gone out the same way, though none of the sources for this event says so.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "52Poké Wiki: SV-P Simplified Chinese promo cards",
